        "code": "gsap_repeated_fromto_without_baseline",
        "severity": "warning",
        "message": "2 tl.fromTo() calls target \"#s2-state-transcribing\" with no stable baseline. The last-authored fromTo \"from\" values become the element's resting state for any seek before the first tween actually runs, because GSAP applies fromTo from-values at authoring time (immediateRender), not at tween position.",
        "selector": "#s2-state-transcribing",
        "dataAttributes": {},
        "sourceFile": "/Users/alihusainsorathiya/Documents/projects/teletype/brag-output/composition/compositions/scene-02.html",
        "bbox": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 0,
          "height": 0
        },
        "time": 0,
        "fixHint": "Add `immediateRender: false` to every fromTo except the earliest-positioned one (at 1.66s), so pre-first-tween seeks keep its \"from\" values. A hiding `tl.set(..., 0)` baseline trips gsap_timeline_set_initial_hide, and a `gsap.set` authored before the fromTo calls is overwritten by them."
      },
      {
        "code": "gsap_non_transform_motion",
        "severity": "error",
        "message": "GSAP tween on \"#s2-caret\" uses motion that snaps to integer device pixels: left. Layout and text-reflow properties snap during browser layout; roundProps rounds the tween value. Slow motion or an ease-out tail then stutters under the seek-by-frame capture engine. Animate transforms (x/y/scale/opacity) instead.",
        "selector": "#s2-caret",
        "dataAttributes": {},
        "sourceFile": "/Users/alihusainsorathiya/Documents/projects/teletype/brag-output/composition/compositions/scene-02.html",
        "bbox": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 0,
          "height": 0
        },
        "time": 0,
        "fixHint": "replace left with the transform equivalent (x), e.g. tl.fromTo(\"#s2-caret\", { x: -1300 }, { x: 0, ...yourAnimation }). Transforms interpolate sub-pixel and stay smooth at any speed."
      }
    ],
